    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C11"],
      "claim": "Ceftriaxone, lacking the alpha-amino acid side chain and bearing a C3 thioheterocycle, has 8% oral bioavailability; this is contradictory but mechanistically less applicable to the query.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high: the query is an oral aminocephalosporin (cefatrizine) with the p-hydroxyphenylglycyl amino side chain shared by amoxicillin, cephradine, cefroxadine, and loracarbef, all with high oral bioavailability. Low-F analogues lack this transporter-recognized amino acid side chain, so the physicochemical permeability prior is overridden by experimental evidence for active intestinal absorption.",
